# Copy to `.env.development.local` (gitignored) for local development.
#
# **`.env.development.local`, not `.env.local`.** Vite loads `.env.local` in
# EVERY mode, including `vite build` — so a developer with local values in it
# who ran the deploy script from their laptop would ship a bundle pointing at
# their own machine. The `.development` infix scopes the file to `vite` (dev
# mode); `vite build` runs in production mode and never reads it.
#
# Both values are baked in at BUILD time, not read at runtime: a deployed bundle
# carries whatever was set when it was built.

# Origin of the scan Worker. Leave UNSET in development: Vite proxies `/api` to
# the local Worker (see vite.config.ts), so a relative path is correct and
# setting this would send local scans to the deployed Worker instead.
# Production sets it in CI, per CONTRIBUTING.md.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://lumioguard-slopmeter-api.<subdomain>.workers.dev

# OPTIONAL. Origin of the LumioGuard app a reading is handed on to.
#
# THE switch for the whole integration. Unset — the default — there is no
# hand-off button, no offer and no LumioGuard wordmark anywhere on the page; the
# tool stands under its own name alone. Set it and all three appear.
#
# Point it at YOUR app, not the deployed one: a site key minted against a local
# database 404s everywhere else, and reads as a broken key rather than a wrong
# address. 5173 is the LumioGuard web app; see CONTRIBUTING.md.
# VITE_LUMIOGUARD_APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
